  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SoftFruit in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Flevoplant B.V. is a specialist in the propagation of strawberry plants. Meteor Systems B.V. produces complete movable cultivation gutter and irrigation systems for greenhouse horticulture, tailored to the specific wishes of the growers and whereby the products can be adapted to the specific (climate) conditions in a specific country. The systems are suitable for large greenhouse complexes, (semi-)outdoor crops and indoor farming and result in higher crop yields and high quality products with minimal consumption of water, fertilisers and energy.Strawberries are already being grown in various areas in Ethiopia, both high and low, especially for export to the Middle East (more than 80%). Production is now mainly done with Israeli strawberry varieties and only in the open ground.With this project, the two Dutch companies want to introduce a new way of strawberry production in Ethiopia in which Dutch strawberry varieties and plants and production methods are applied: increased cultivation on substrate in gutters and a mini-air system for climate and temperature regulation. The two Dutch companies want to demonstrate that their technology increases production, reduces costs and reduces the use of pesticides, fertilisers and water.The demonstration project will take place at the Zuqualla Horti Farm. Zuqualla is a company that grows flowers and cultivates 22 hectares of strawberries in the open field, which means that an efficiency gain is missed. Zuqualla is located in an area where other horticultural companies are located that can visit the demonstration project.This project therefore involves the production of high-quality strawberries, a large part of which is destined for export. The application of Dutch technologies will therefore strengthen Ethiopia&apos;s competitive position internationally.</narrative>
  </description>
